\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar eases at start of wait-and-see week. \b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2000\par 22:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  CANADA OPEN  1.5037    PREVIOUS CLOSE  1.5035\par \tab \tab  DAILY  HIGH  1.5110    OVERNIGHT HIGH  1.5060\par \tab \tab \tab    LOW  1.5025\tab \tab    LOW  1.5022\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      By Ka Yan Ng \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Oct 2 (Reuters) - Recent merger and acquisition \par \par \uc2  activity pushed the Canadian dollar lower on Monday, in what is \par \par \uc2  largely seen as the beginning of a wait-and-see week with a \par \par \uc2  raft of key economic events waiting in the wings, said market \par \par \uc2  watchers. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar closed at C$1.5101 (66.22 U.S. cents) \par \par \uc2  on Monday against C$1.5035 (66.51 U.S. cents) from the previous \par \par \uc2  session's close. \par \par \uc2  "It's weakened today. There's been a a lot of discussion \par \par \uc2  about different (merger and acquisition) things going through," \par \par \uc2  said Andy Busch, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BMO Nesbitt \par \par \uc2  Burns Inc. in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  He pointed to recent deals such as Royal Bank of Canada \par \par \uc2   buying U.S. securities firm Dain Rauscher Corp. \par \par \uc2  and Premdor Inc. snapping up International Paper's \par \par \uc2   Masonite building materials unit. \par \par \uc2  Though the Canadian dollar has not weakened primarily on \par \par \uc2  the back of such deals, Busch said, "it's certainly kept the \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar quite bid." \par \par \uc2  As the Canadian dollar saw its value chipped away over the \par \par \uc2  past week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is feeling both cautious and \par \par \uc2  marking time ahead of new data or events, said market players. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has fallen from C$1.4886 (67.18 U.S. \par \par \uc2  cents) on September 22 - the day the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined \par \par \uc2  international \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the euro - to close at \par \par \uc2  C$1.5035 (66.51 U.S. cents) last Friday, hovering around \par \par \uc2  four-month lows in the process. \par \par \uc2      "After last week and the previous Friday, there's a lot of \par \par \uc2  cautiousness in the marketplace," said Busch. \par \par \uc2      Market players shrugged off the release on Monday of the \par \par \uc2  U.S. National Association of Purchasing Managers' index for \par \par \uc2  September that showed it had contracted for the second straight \par \par \uc2  month. \par \par \uc2  Instead, dealers are looking ahead to Tuesday's meeting of \par \par \uc2  the U.S. Federal Reserve. The Fed is widely expected to leave \par \par \uc2  its interest rate policies unchanged. \par \par \uc2      A series of other economic data and events has the Canadian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a cautious mood. \par \par \uc2      "I think it's just a wait-and-see kind of deal," said \par \par \uc2  Busch. \par \par \uc2      The upcoming economic data include both Canada and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  employment reports for September on Friday, although otherwise \par \par \uc2  the week is fairly light on domestic data. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, both the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \par \par \uc2  England are also scheduled to meet this week. \par \par \uc2      In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 72.12 yen compared with 71.87 at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at C$1.3227 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus C$1.3226. The Canadian dollar was at \par \par \uc2  A$1.2113 against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2250. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa205oa9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
