\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar hits four-month lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2000\par 23:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  CANADA OPEN  1.4895    PREVIOUS CLOSE  1.4874\par \tab \tab  DAILY  HIGH  1.4974    OVERNIGHT HIGH  1.4935\par \tab \tab \tab    LOW  1.4864\tab \tab    LOW  1.4864\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      By Ka Yan Ng \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar hit a \par \par \uc2  four-month low on Wednesday as a raft of factors weighed on the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a historic Danish referendum to decide on \par \par \uc2  joining the euro. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar closed at C$1.4962 (66.84 U.S. cents) \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday against C$1.4874 (67.23 U.S. cents) from the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close. At midday, the Canadian dollar \par \par \uc2  dropped to C$1.4974, a level not touched since May 31. \par \par \uc2  Cross selling of the Canadian unit against the euro, and \par \par \uc2  selling pressures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the IMM, the Chicago-based \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, were the primary reason the Canadian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drooped in early dealings. \par \par \uc2  Some market watchers said an investor newsletter by Dennis \par \par \uc2  Gartman further undermined the Canadian dollar when he \par \par \uc2  recommended investors sell Canadian equities. \par \par \uc2  "Mr. Gartman has been a huge bull on Canada, and he threw \par \par \uc2  in a sell recommendation on the TSE today, which I think \par \par \uc2  probably compounded the weakness we're seeing in both the TSE \par \par \uc2  and the Canadian dollar," said one senior Canadian economist. \par \par \uc2      "When things are already sort of pulling backwards, \par \par \uc2  somebody else piling on doesn't help matters," he added. \par \par \uc2      But, other analysts were sceptical of the impact of \par \par \uc2  Gartman's newsletter on the market. \par \par \uc2      "There are a whole lot of underpinnings here. The CPI \par \par \uc2  revision in the U.S., their two-year auction today, equity \par \par \uc2  swooning... it's hard to hang it all on one factor. My lowest \par \par \uc2  choice for that is the investor newsletter," said Jeoff Hall, \par \par \uc2  managing Canadian market analyst at Thomson IFR. \par \par \uc2      The Toronto Stock Exchange Composite 300 Index fell 228.60 \par \par \uc2  points, or 2.18 percent, to close at 10,250.00 as Nortel \par \par \uc2  Networks Corp., which represents about one-third of the index, \par \par \uc2  felt the heat from other battered technology shares who have \par \par \uc2  recently issued profit warnings. \par \par \uc2      Some market watchers said the losses on the TSE were \par \par \uc2  weighing on the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "I believe very strongly that one of the major components \par \par \uc2  helping the Canadian dollar over the time that Aussie has been \par \par \uc2  weakening has been the desire by equity fund managers to have \par \par \uc2  exposure - indicated everytime we came up near C$1.500 or \par \par \uc2  C$1.4930, they bought Canadian dollars and U.S. dollars went \par \par \uc2  lower," said Andy Busch, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BMO \par \par \uc2  Nesbitt Burns Inc. in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. government said on Wednesday that a computer \par \par \uc2  glitch had caused it to mismeasure the main U.S. inflation \par \par \uc2  gauge, the Consumer Price Index, and that it was taking the \par \par \uc2  unusual step of revising past data. More details would be \par \par \uc2  released at a 9:30 a.m. (1330 GMT) briefing on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market watchers now turn the spotlight to Denmark where a \par \par \uc2  referendum will take place to decide whether the country will \par \par \uc2  adopt the euro. Market players will also be tracking \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements in case there is another coordinated global \par \par \uc2  effort to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the euro in case there is a \par \par \uc2  "no" vote. \par \par \uc2      "That's really what's going to be the focus of the entire \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  world tomorrow," said Busch. \par \par \uc2      "You can see the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \par \par \uc2  Canadian dollar to buy euros and sell Canadian dollars which \par \par \uc2  should be really interesting given that we are at the highs. So \par \par \uc2  there is some question mark as to whether or they will want to \par \par \uc2  do that," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar traded at the high end of its range on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday and market watchers said further weakening is \par \par \uc2  possible. \par \par \uc2  "My guess is should we clear the C$1.50 hurdle, we'll see \par \par \uc2  C$1.5050 fairly quickly," said Busch, noting no big event is \par \par \uc2  necessary, just investors will stop buying Canadian dollars at \par \par \uc2  C$1.4900. \par \par \uc2      Month end pressures were also cited as another negative for \par \par \uc2  the embattled Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2      Canadian gross domestic product data for July, scheduled \par \par \uc2  for release on Friday, is the only significant Canadian data \par \par \uc2  expected this week. \par \par \uc2      In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 71.78 yen compared to 72.38 at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at C$1.3197 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus C$1.3112. The Canadian dollar was at A$1.2141 \par \par \uc2   against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2252. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9r064rc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
