\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar dips as market watchers eye euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2000\par 22:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  CANADA OPEN  1.4865    PREVIOUS CLOSE  1.4870\par \tab \tab  DAILY  HIGH  1.4890    OVERNIGHT HIGH  1.4884\par \tab \tab \tab    LOW  1.4855\tab \tab    LOW  1.4860\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      By Ka Yan Ng \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar dipped \par \par \uc2  slightly on Tuesday but remained in its recent range with the \par \par \uc2  threat of euro \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the minds of some short-staffed \par \par \uc2  trading desks. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at C$1.4874 (67.23 U.S. cents) on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday against C$1.4870 (67.25 U.S. cents) from the previous \par \par \uc2  session's close. \par \par \uc2  Trading desks were short-staffed on Tuesday as the Treasury \par \par \uc2  Management Association of Canada conference in Vancouver caused \par \par \uc2  less-than-normal liquidity in the Canadian dollar and will \par \par \uc2  likely continue until the conference concludes, said market \par \par \uc2  players. \par \par \uc2  But there was some interest to sell Canadian dollars at the \par \par \uc2  C$1.4840-50 area on the International Monetary Market, the \par \par \uc2  Chicago-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market, and also from corporate \par \par \uc2  sellers, said traders. \par \par \uc2  "We saw some interest on option contracts, but by and large \par \par \uc2  it was relatively a quiet day," said Jack Spitz, regional \par \par \uc2  manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at National Bank of Canada. \par \par \uc2  "It's been trading the range and interest in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  on either side of the range really doesn't exist. There is good \par \par \uc2  corporate support for Canada at C$1.4920," he added, noting \par \par \uc2  that the range was narrowing and will likely break soon. \par \par \uc2      The $1.4850 area represents a fairly significant technical \par \par \uc2  level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one Toronto \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2      But the C$1.4850 level may prove more of a psychological \par \par \uc2  level, with real resistance looming in the C$1.4830-35 area, he \par \par \uc2  added. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, some of the focus in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets \par \par \uc2  revolve around euro activity. There are still fears lingering \par \par \uc2  that another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may occur soon \par \par \uc2  after the surprise coordinated global effort from central banks \par \par \uc2  to shore up the euro's value. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty over the outcome of Thursday's Danish \par \par \uc2  referendum on joining the euro was also adding some pressure, \par \par \uc2  said traders. \par \par \uc2  "If you see some movement for the euro to get stronger, I \par \par \uc2  think the initial reaction would be to sell Canada. You might \par \par \uc2  see some unwinding of some euro-Canada positions," said Spitz. \par \par \uc2  But, he noted that the Canadian dollar was relatively \par \par \uc2  unscathed last week after the surprise move by the Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to join in the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro continues to travel higher, then I think maybe \par \par \uc2  a little bit of pressure on Canada, but I don't see great \par \par \uc2  pressure," he said. \par \par \uc2  Canadian gross domestic product data for July, scheduled \par \par \uc2  for release on Friday, is the only significant data expected \par \par \uc2  this week. \par \par \uc2  In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 72.38 yen compared to 72.40 at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at C$1.3112 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus C$1.2987. The Canadian dollar was at A$1.2252 \par \par \uc2   against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2228. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9q06g8o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
