\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  joins euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday joined central banks from Europe, Japan and the United States in the fight to defend the beleaguered euro on the eve of a meeting of the Group of Seven industrialised countries. \par \par \uc2  "Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  joins concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys euro versus Canadian dollars," said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Bank officials declined to confirm if the bank had used its own funds to buy euros for Canadian dollars and said they will not be making any further comment on Friday. \par \par \uc2  G7 finance ministers are gathering in Prague this weekend for the annual meetings of the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Analysts cheered the move by the Bank of Canada and its counterparts ahead of the meeting of G7 finance ministers. \par \par \uc2  "In a way, that was a brilliant stroke. I think the market was assuming we'd wait and see what came out of the G7 meeting and they were probably ready to pounce on it and say it wasn't enough," said Doug Porter, senior economist at BMO Nesbitt Burns Inc. \par \par \uc2  "I think it really caught the the market flat-footed," he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  effort since 1995, drove the euro up sharply before relinquishing some of its early gains. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the concerted move by central banks sent a positive message to euro markets. \par \par \uc2  "I think the Bank of Canada was just trying to show some solidarity. I don't think they were at all concerned about the specific Canadian dollar-euro exchange rate, that's not really a huge issue for the Canadian economy," said Porter. \par \par \uc2  "In a way it shows how strong the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is versus units other than the U.S. dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar opened at C$1.4900 (67.11 U.S. cents) on Friday against C$1.4865 (67.27 U.S. cents) at the previous session's close. Traders said early morning trading activity was "very busy," taking the Canadian dollar to 1.3194 against the euro, on news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06k9a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
