\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dollar sags, central banks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 17:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CANADA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPEN  1.4900    PREVIOUS CLOSE  1.4837\par \tab \tab  DAILY  HIGH  1.4920    OVERNIGHT HIGH  1.4921\par \tab \tab \tab    LOW  1.4885\tab \tab    LOW  1.4867\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TORONTO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar weakened \par \par \uc2  on Friday on news of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the \par \par \uc2  euro by Group of Seven central banks ahead of G7 meetings in \par \par \uc2  Prague this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar was at C$1.4910 (67.07 U.S. cents) in \par \par \uc2  late morning on Friday against C$1.4865 (67.27 U.S. cents) at \par \par \uc2  the close on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada on Friday joined central banks from \par \par \uc2  Europe, Japan and the United States in the fight to defend the \par \par \uc2  beleaguered euro. \par \par \uc2  "Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  joins concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys euro versus Canadian dollars," said the Canadian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Canadian dollar was in the C$1.4862 area \par \par \uc2  ahead of confirmation from the central banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  and weakened as low as C$1.4920 in under an hour of frenetic \par \par \uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  "Surprisingly, the Canadian dollar has held up quite well \par \par \uc2  considering the fact that the Bank of Canada is participating \par \par \uc2  in the concerted effort to support the euro by the other \par \par \uc2  central banks," said Steve Demers, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  at National Bank of Canada. \par \par \uc2      "The Canadian dollar volatility has been surprisingly low \par \par \uc2  in a sense," he added. \par \par \uc2      Demers said there was good two-way flows between the \par \par \uc2  Canadian and U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as in euro-U.S. cross \par \par \uc2  trades. \par \par \uc2      Analysts were cheered by the concerted move, calling it a \par \par \uc2  show of "international solidarity." But the euro needs to close \par \par \uc2  higher for the confidence to remain. \par \par \uc2      "Now the big question is whether the central banks will \par \par \uc2  come back into the market to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make sure the euro \par \par \uc2  does close today at a higher level," said Demers. \par \par \uc2      "Should there be more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you can probably \par \par \uc2  expect to a little bit more weakness in the Canadian dollar," \par \par \uc2  he added. \par \par \uc2      In cross-trading against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian \par \par \uc2  dollar was at 72.35 yen, compared with 71.70 at the \par \par \uc2  previous session's close, and at 1.3164 against the euro \par \par \uc2   versus 1.2754. The Canadian dollar was at A$1.2165 \par \par \uc2   against the Australian dollar versus A$1.2346. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06jmu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
