\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Euro to feature in G7 communique- \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2 's Martin. \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2000\par 20:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  PRAGUE, Sept 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro reflected concern about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Canada joined in because it benefits from stable markets, Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Martin, in Prague to attend Saturday's meeting of the Group of Seven industrialised countries and the annual meetings of the World Bank and International Monetary Fund, told reporters that both oil and the euro would feature in the G7 discussions after Friday's shock \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , abstractly, is something that always exists, but essentially it is not something that you discuss in advance," Martin said. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously there were concerns (about the euro), which is why the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place, so I think you can assume that the communique will make some mention of this." \par \par \uc2  He added, "\b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  participated in this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we have a great deal to gain by stability in world markets." \par \par \uc2  Central banks sold dollars and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for euros on Friday ahead of the G7 meeting after mounting concern from Europeans about the impact of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparently relentless slide. The action drained euros from the market and gave the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  support. \par \par \uc2  Martin said high oil prices would also be on the agenda at the G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  "We would obviously like to see the prices be of a level that do not cause the kind of disruptions we have seen. At the same time we want to see prices that are sustainable over a longer period," he said. \par \par \uc2  Current problems were caused both by strong demand in a booming world economy and by tight supply, he added. \par \par \uc2  Martin said he also planned to use his time in Prague for bilateral talks with ministers from the Group of 20 developed and developing countries. \par \par \uc2  The group meets in Montreal next month to review progress in reforming and improving the world financial system after the crisis which struck Asia and other regions in 1997-99. \par \par \uc2  It is the second meeting of the new group - the first one took place in Berlin late last year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9m06fqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
