\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Duisenberg sees weak euro as inflation risk. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jeffrey Jones \par \uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2000\par 00:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CALGARY, Sept 8 (Reuters) - Europe's top central banker Friday minced no words in saying the euro's tumble to record lows against the dollar this week was not justified and warning long-term euro weakness could spark inflation. \par \par \uc2  Sticking to the message already broadcast by European finance ministers and his \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  colleague Christian Noyer in France, Duisenberg said talk there was no end in sight to the euro's losses was "clear nonsense." \par \par \uc2  "The actual exchange rate is clearly out of line with the underlying fundamental relationship and there must and will come a point when the relationship will change in the direction of a more justified relationship," Duisenberg told business leaders. \par \par \uc2  But even this high profile verbal defence of the euro left investors cold and the euro ended the week off nearly four cents at 86.60 cents, just a whisker above the all time lows it hit near 86.30 cents Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The more they talk, the more the market is going to sell the euro," said UBS Warburg chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Jeremy Fand as news wires light up with fresh comments about the euro. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg, noting the ECB's mandate is to maintain price stability, also explained a weak euro's knock-on effect on the economy could be strong and analysts said leaders would be most worried about how the rising cost for oil, denominated in dollars, could choke off growth. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, Duisenberg said it was critical to maintain confidence in the still sliding euro. The European common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has plunged more than 25 percent since its launch in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  For months European leaders have said the euro's decline was more related to the U.S. economy's ongoing strong performance rather than Europe's weaker growth potential. \par \par \uc2  But now that European companies are pressing ahead with restructuring - and reaping stronger growth because of it - they have begun to protest that fundamentals are out of line. \par \par \uc2  In his Calgary remarks, however, Duisenberg failed to address market speculation about how the ECB may act to stem the euro's persistent slide, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up. \par \par \uc2  Members of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's business and political elite attending the speech said they were still in the dark about the ECB's next step. \par \par \uc2  "I don't take what Duisenberg said as a signal they may or may not take action," said Tony Comper, chief executive officer of Bank of Montreal, Canada's fifth largest bank. "Like everything else, things have to unfold and markets will react as they think appropriate." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been inundated with talk about the euro this week, especially after Germany's Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder said earlier in the week he was unconcerned by its fall. Though he later took back the statement, the damage had already been done, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In his speech, Duisenberg said international investors would have to believe the euro was a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before they agreed to use it to hold assets in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  "Only if investors outside the euro area are confident that their purchasing power will be preserved over time, will they engage in euro-denominated financial activities," he said. \par \par \uc2  His comments came as the euro hovered around $0.8654 - a little above its record lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9808kbv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
