\par\par \b \uc2  Canada dollar ends flat after morning slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 22:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab   CANADA OPEN 1.5119\tab   ASIA   HIGH  1.5123\par \tab   PREV  CLOSE 1.5077\tab \tab   LOW  1.5055\par \tab   DAILY HIGH  1.5130\tab   EUROPE HIGH  1.5122\par \tab \tab  LOW  1.5071\tab \tab   LOW  1.5077\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2     TORONTO, March 25 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar closed \par \par \uc2  almost unchanged on Thursday at C$1.5076 ($0.663), bouncing in \par \par \uc2  a rocky session but ending flat after speculation the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Canada was prepared to trim interest rates proved false. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Canadian dollar, a victim of recent \par \par \uc2  rate-cut talk in part because of Canada's minuscule inflation \par \par \uc2  levels, firmed from its morning lows as the Bank of Canada left \par \par \uc2  interest rates unchanged. \par \par \uc2     The Bank of Canada usually moves to adjust interest rates \par \par \uc2  at, or slightly before, 0900 EST/1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2     Traders said the market will likely be cautious toward the \par \par \uc2  Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at least until Canadian and U.S. near-term \par \par \uc2  monetary policies are better defined. The Federal Open Market \par \par \uc2  Committee will meet on March 30, with only a small percentage \par \par \uc2  of analysts expecting a Fed interest rate hike. \par \par \uc2     Few analysts expect the Bank of Canada (BOC) to trim rates, \par \par \uc2  especially before the FOMC's meeting. \par \par \uc2     The BOC said on Thursday it will start announcing when it \par \par \uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maximize the impact of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2     Deputy Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Charles Freedman told \par \par \uc2  reporters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  through \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokers in a bid to "maintain the effectiveness of the \par \par \uc2  signal". \par \par \uc2     The BOC last year scrapped its method of automatically \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy or sell dollars at set levels. \par \par \uc2     No major economic releases are expected from Canada or the \par \par \uc2  United States on Friday. \par \par \uc2     On the crosses, Canada's dollar ended flat against the yen \par \par \uc2  at 78.34 from 78.27. The dollar was slightly firmer against the \par \par \uc2  euro at C$1.6321 from C$1.6383. \par \par \uc2      ((Jason Hopps, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8105, \par \par \uc2  toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv3p087nk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
