\par\par \b \uc2  =Canada $2.5B Global Bond Caps Campaign To Boost  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Evans \par \uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1998\par 21:09\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The $2.5 billion global bond offering launched by Canada into international credit markets Tuesday was the keynote issue of an aggressive campaign to replenish an international reserve account drained by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the summer, analysts and government sources said. \par \par \uc2  The 10-year issue, which carried a coupon of 5.25% and offered a spread of 67 basis points over U.S. Treasurys, was Canada's largest-ever public offering of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated bonds, Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials told Dow Jones Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The issue is seen as the culmination of a recent pattern of aggressive Canadian government issuance that has also included a four-billion French franc, a 4.45% 10-year issue, and a 200 million pound sterling re-opening of Canada's 6.25% medium-term note. Canada also mounted a four billion deutsche mark-denominated 10-year issue in late June. \par \par \uc2  All proceeds from these issues have been applied to boosting the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, in accordance with long-standing government practice with regard to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated issues. \par \par \uc2  Canada's official international reserves were seriously depleted by repeated Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the Canadian dollar through the summer. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cost the government $5.8 billion in the month of August alone, bringing reserves down to $17.9 billion by the end of August. \par \par \uc2  At the time, the finance ministry indicated it would seek to top boost reserves "to reflect increased flows and volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," and most analysts concede that Tuesday's $2.5 billion global did the trick quite nicely, although the issue's settlement date of November 5 means that proceeds from the deal will not appear in October's reserve figures. \par \par \uc2  According to estimates from Standard and Poor's MMS in Toronto, the recent slate of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuance should help boost Canada's international reserves to a new record amount of about $23 billion by November. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  10-27-98 \par \par \uc2  1509EST \par \par \uc2  4228 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916duar02ii8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
