\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of Canada -2: Analysts See Earlier Policy As Failure \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1998\par 18:43\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The formal change in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy comes after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more frequently and aggressively than normal policy dictated when the Canadian dollar came under particularly intense attack in August. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had previously deviated from the policy during times of acute pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it did so with particular emphasis during the August assault on the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At the same time, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sometimes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in accordance with its normal policy. \par \par \uc2  Some Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market watchers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move was inevitable after what they described as an ultimately failed effort to contain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The biggest (reason for the change) is because the methodology they were working with before really didn't have a chance of working," said Mark Chandler, an economist with Goldman Sachs in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  Chandler characterized the policy change as a retreat from an ambitious but flawed experiment. \par \par \uc2  "I think it was bit of an experiment. It was an ambitious task they set themselves to see if they could control intraday volatility in such a fashion," he said. \par \par \uc2  But because of the predictability of the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it became a "near-term speed bump" that was well-recognized and wasn't effective, Chandler said. \par \par \uc2  Bill Mooney, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with Societe Generale, agreed that the predictability of the bank's old approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended up undermining its effectiveness. \par \par \uc2  "It kind of defeats the whole purpose of trying to defend something when you take away the element of surprise," Mooney said. \par \par \uc2  Pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves may also have contributed to its decision to opt for less structured approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mooney suggested. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record US$5.82 billion defending the embattled Canadian dollar in August alone, taking its reserves to US$17.97 billion. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  09-30-98 \par \par \uc2  1243EDT \par \par \uc2  4232 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du9u02bxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
