\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Opts For "Discretionary"  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Style \b0\par\par\uc2  By Don Curren \par \uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1998\par 18:17\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has abandoned its policy of regular, predictable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in defense of the Canadian dollar in favor of a more discretionary approach, bank officials confirmed Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The decision by the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the federal department of finance marks the formal abandonment of the bank's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets whenever the U.S. dollar moved 70 ticks against the Canadian dollar in either direction from the previous day's official close. \par \par \uc2  The policy, first adopted by the bank in April 1995, was intended to smooth out volatility in Canadian dollar trading. \par \par \uc2  An official statement on the change said it is intended to increase the effectiveness and "signaling impact" of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Bank and the department of finance have decided to make further changes to the way \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is conducted in the market for the Canadian dollar," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  "From now on, the bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a more discretionary manner, as it did in August, in order to increase the signaling impact and effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The purpose of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains promotion of orderly markets," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada referred further inquiries on the change to a finance department who was not available for comment late Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  True to its word, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood on the sidelines Wednesday morning as the Canadian dollar tumbled through what would have been the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger of C$1.5175. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, which closed at C$1.5105 Tuesday, climbed as high as C$1.5310 before relinquishing some of its gains. It was at C$1.5259 at 12:09 p.m. EDT (1609 GMT). \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  09-30-98 \par \par \uc2  1217EDT \par \par \uc2  4232 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du9u02bwe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
