\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: First Action This Month \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1998\par 21:33\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday afternoon, selling\par U.S. dollars at C$1.5090 in an effort to smooth out trading\par action, said a trader in Toronto.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  halted the U.S. dollar's ascent, and\par it was trading at C$1.5090 at 3:23 p.m. EDT (1923 GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was consistent with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par unofficial policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets when\par the U.S. dollar moves 70 ticks against the Canadian dollar\par either way on an intraday basis. The U.S. dollar closed at\par C$1.5017 Tuesday.\par    The action is believed to have been the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since Aug. 31, when it reportedly sold\par U.S. dollars at C$1.5675.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in August, often\par departing from its policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 70-tick\par intraday moves, while the Canadian dollar was under severe\par pressure as a result of declining commodity markets and\par global financial turbulence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    But the bank has apparently been absent from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets so far in September. The Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par bounced back vigorously this month, although some analysts\par believe it is vulnerable to global financial pressures and\par could once again head significantly lower.\par    The Canadian dollar was relatively stable for most of\par the day, but began to weaken in the afternoon after a\par speech by U.S. Federal Reserve Board Chairman Alan\par Greenspan.\par    Greenspan told U.S. legislators there is no move afoot\par for a coordinated interest rate cut among G-7 nations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  09-16-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1533EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du9g026y6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
