\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Moves Reduced  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Reserves In August \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 16:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones Online News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  OTTAWA -(Dow Jones)-  Canadian monetary reserves fell $4.56 billion in August, the Canadian Finance Department said Thursday, as government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to defend the besieged Canadian dollar reduced reserves by nearly $6 billion. \par \par \uc2  As of Aug. 31, the official holdings of gold, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other monetary assets totaled $17.97 billion, down from $22.52 billion in July and down from $20.08 billion a year earlier. All reserve figures are reported in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A survey of Canadian economists by Technical Data had estimated August reserves at $17.86 billion. \par \par \uc2  The department said official government \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced reserves by $5.82 billion in August. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets repeatedly in August and \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised official interest rates in an attempt to support the embattled Canadian dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has suffered from fundamental weakness stemming from lower short-term interest rates compared to those in the U.S., low commodity prices and global uncertainty stemming from economic and financial turmoil in Asia and Russia. \par \par \uc2  "It's not as if it's a shock that the government spent a lot of money defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Doug Porter, senior economist at Nesbitt Burns Inc. The largest decline in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings before August was the US$3.2 billion drop in September 1992, he pointed out. \par \par \uc2  "This is right off the radar screen in terms of dollar defense," Porter said. "It gives you a sense of just how vigorously the bank was trying to defend the (Canadian) dollar during the month, and it shows to what extent they were going to before they finally succumbed and raised rates." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its bellwether bank rate 100 basis points to 6.00% on Aug. 27 in a move designed to provide support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and maintain suitable monetary conditions for noninflationary growth. \par \par \uc2  "Canada retains a strong reserve position," the Finance Department said Thursday. It said it will continue its policy, as outlined in recent budgets, of increasing reserves to reflect increased flows and volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The government plans to replenish reserves through a broad range of financing programs, it said. The management of reserves is supported by the recent extension of Canada's $6 billion standby line of credit with international banks, the department said. \par \par \uc2  Official government \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August also included a loan to Thailand, which reduced reserves by $361 million. \par \par \uc2  While some analysts argue that Canada's reserves are adequate by international market standards, Hall said the recent developments in the account raise questions about the extent of the holdings. "Among industrialized nations, the amount of reserves that Canada had was on the low side, Japan being the very other extreme," he said. \par \par \uc2  While the reserve account had been building by about US$175 million a month for most of the last three years, that trend has been arrested in recent months, Hall said. \par \par \uc2  Ottawa must start to rebuild the account, TechData's Hall suggested. \par \par \uc2  Nesbitt's Porter agreed that efforts to increase the war chest are likely in the coming months. "They don't seem to have any specific target for the level of reserves,' Porter said." (But) it seems that something on the order of US$20 billion can be used as a benchmark, so one way or another they will likely try to rebuild those reserves over the next six to 12 months.' \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  4342 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020329du9301731\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
