\par\par \b \uc2  =Record Drop In Canada  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Foreseen By Analysts \b0\par\par\uc2  By Don Curren \par \uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1998\par 17:11\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--While the Bank of Canada spent a\par record US$5.82 billion defending the besieged Canadian\par dollar in August, market watchers were prepared for high\par levels of spending and greeted the news with little\par surprise Thursday morning.\par    The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unusually aggressive style of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in August had prepared market\par watchers for a large figure, and estimates of the total net\par decrease of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings had ranged from US$2\par billion to US$7 billion.\par    The finance department, which handles the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve accounts, announced\par Thursday morning that the the reserves fell US$4.56 billion\par in August to US$17.97 billion from US$22.52 billion in July\par after the effects of various reserve-building \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par were taken into account.\par    "It's not as if it's a shock that the government spent\par a lot of money defending the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Doug Porter,\par senior economist at Nesbitt Burns Inc.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The largest decline in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings before\par August was the US$3.2 billion drop in September 1992, he\par pointed out.\par    "This is right off the radar screen in terms of dollar\par defense," Porter said. "It gives you a sense of just how\par vigorously the bank was trying to defend the (Canadian)\par dollar during the month, and it shows to what extent they\par were going to before they finally succumbed and raised\par rates."\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised its bellwether bank rate 100\par basis points to 6.00% on Aug. 27 in a move it said was\par designed to provide support for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as well as\par maintain suitable monetary conditions for non-inflationary\par growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  09-03-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1111EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4225 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du930246l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
