\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dollar closes weaker after bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1998\par 22:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar closed weaker at C$1.5674 (US$0.6379) on Monday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the troubled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought Canadian dollars at levels from C$1.5675 (US$0.6379) to C$1.5730 (US$0.6357) as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened past key support levels. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian dollar stabilised and was eventually sidelined by falling equity markets. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has suffered from turmoil in international markets, particularly in Russia, which prompted fears that a global economic downturn would spread from emerging markets to more developed Western economies. \par \par \uc2  But that turmoil jolted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets more severely on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Toronto Stock Exchange's composite 300 index fell by about four percent to close at 5530.66, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average dropped 6.4 percent to close at 7539.07 \par \par \uc2  "I think obviously the stock market (the Dow) has deflected concerns about the Canadian dollar right now," said Jeoff Hall, managing Canadian market analyst with Thomson Global Markets. \par \par \uc2  Equity markets were spooked by news that Russia's opposition communists would reject President Boris Yeltsin's choice of Viktor Chernomyrdin as the country's next prime minister. A senior Kremlin aide also warned of possible political revolution in Russia. \par \par \uc2  Western nations have called on Russian President Boris Yeltsin to implement strong reforms to cope with a financial crisis that threatens to topple Russia's economy. \par \par \uc2  Hall said the weaker U.S. equity markets could end up haunting the Canadian dollar if economic growth slows in the United States and Americans begin buying fewer Canadian exports. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the release of economic data failed to have an impact on the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Statistics Canada reported Canada's real gross domestic product fell 0.1 percent in June after falling 0.3 percent in the previous month. \par \par \uc2  The agency also said Canada's current account deficit narrowed marginally in the second quarter to C$4.23 billion from a C$4.28 billion deficit in the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  A Reuters survey of economists had forecast a 0.2 percent decline in monthly GDP and a current account deficit of C$4.79 billion. \par \par \uc2  "The data had little impact overall. The most important piece of it was the current account and there was little change," said Rob Palombi, senior fixed-income analyst with Standard & Poor's MMS International. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said growing speculation the U.S. Federal Reserve might cut interest rates was helping to keep Canadian dollar buyers in the market. \par \par \uc2  London markets were closed today for a bank holiday. \par \par \uc2  In cross trading, the Canadian dollar fell to 1.1123 German marks from Friday's close of 1.1251 marks and dropped to 88.91 yen from 90.73 yen at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8104) or email: \par \par \uc2  toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8v01uhf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal