\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1998\par 18:02\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market repeatedly Monday morning,\par selling U.S. dollars at various levels including C$1.5695\par after first coming into the market at C$1.5675, said a\par trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar leveled off briefly after the first\par stages of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and then resumed its upwards\par climb. It was at C$1.5735 at 12:01 p.m. EDT (1601 GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of\par 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The U.S.\par dollar closed at C$1.5605 on Friday.\par    In cases of sustained pressure against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par Bank will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly at each five-tick level.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market sources reported seeing a pattern of\par repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday morning\par after the first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at C$1.5675 around 11:15 a.m.\par EDT (1515 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-31-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1202EDT \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8v021jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
