\par\par \b \uc2  Canada $ Plummets -2: Rate Hike Seen Totally Ineffective \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1998\par 16:58\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Canada's 100-basis\par point raising of its benchmark bank rate Thursday has failed\par to alleviate the massive pressure stacked up against the\par Canadian dollar, with the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now having\par fallen more than 150 ticks from its Wednesday close against\par the U.S. dollar.\par    After reaching as high as C$1.5840 earlier, the U.S.\par dollar was trading at C$1.5780 at 10:52 a.m. EDT (1452 GMT),\par from C$1.5750 at 8 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and C$1.5648 late\par Wednesday.\par    Traders said there has been sporadic and inconsistent\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Canadian unit's favor from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  throughout the morning, but these salvos have\par so far had no effect in stemming the bleeding for the\par Canadian dollar.\par    The bank was seen selling U.S. dollars beginning at\par C$1.5630, and at several other apparently random levels as\par the U.S. dollar continued climbing higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Several \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders described the speed of the\par Canadian dollar's fall Thursday as "frightening," saying\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics have completely lost\par their credibility and effectiveness with Thursday's\par ill-timed rate hike.\par    "Whatever the bank's spent on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today, trust\par me, they've spent far more in credibility," said one\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader. "All the rate hike did was give offshore\par accounts better levels to sell their Canadian assets.\par Accounts are making a lot of money today at the expense of\par inadequate policy decisions."\par    Many said the overwhelming pressure against the Canadian\par dollar will not relent appreciably as long as worldwide\par commodity prices continue to fall, as in the mind of the\par market, the value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is closely linked to the\par value of commodities.\par    Some said there is also considerable speculation that\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may soon have to institute another, smaller\par hike in rates to try and stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-27-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1058EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8r01z2y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
