\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar hits record lows, bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar fell to a record low of C$1.5600 (US$0.6410) on Wednesday as nervous investors reacted to continued financial turmoil in Russia, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Russia's rouble fell another 40.8 percent in value against the German mark. The troubled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also fell five percent against the U.S. dollar before the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange declared the day's spot dollar trade against the rouble void. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the Russian economy is collapsing, so that is leading to more volatility abroad," said Mario Angastiniotis, economist with Standard & Poor's MMS International. \par \par \uc2  The renewed sell-off of the Canadian dollar prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and try to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has spent an estimated $3.5 billion out of its $20 billion in foreign reserves buying Canadian dollars in August. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought Canadian dollars at levels from C$1.5560 (US$0.6426) and C$1.5595 (US$0.6412). \par \par \uc2  "They're coming in with the usual amount," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a Canadian bank. \par \par \uc2  The Canada unit has lost 10 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar in the past six months and markets appear poised to continue the sell-off until the Bank of Canada raises interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the likelihood of a rate hike had risen. \par \par \uc2  In cross trading, the Canadian dollar dipped to 1.1576 German marks from Monday's close of 1.1606 and fell to 92.49 yen from 93.03 yen at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  ($1=$1.56 Canadian) \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Simao, Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8104) or email: toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01k8u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
