\par\par \b \uc2  Toronto stocks down one percent at noon. \b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 18:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab     CHANGE\tab \tab \tab   CHANGE\par TSE300     6190.83  -65.18 HI 6192.36\tab    LO 6166.53\par DJIA\tab 8549.87  -52.78 GOLD (LONDON)   US$283.15 +0.10\par FTSE\tab 5545.40 -109.00 GOLD (COMEX)   US$287.50 +0.60\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  NIKKEI    14866.03 -206.90 LME CASH NICKEL US$3995    -84 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANDLR\tab 1.5623\tab  LME CASH ALUM   US$1319   -11.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CAN 30-YR   130.24   -1.69 BRENT CRUDE    US$12.45  -0.23\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------MARKET COMMENT-------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Toronto stocks were down one percent in noon trading on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday as investors reacted to the Russia's continuing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic crisis and Canada's slumping dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 26 (Reuters) - Toronto stocks were down more than one percent in noon trading on Wednesday as investors continued to react with caution to Russia's unfolding economic problems and Canada's falling dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Toronto Stock Exchange's key 300 Composite Index fell 65.18 points or 1.04 percent to 6190.83. Volume was 39.3 million shares worth C$773.5 million. Decliners were outpacing advancers 619 to 158 with another 245 issues on the sidelines unchanged.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It was a similar story in New York, where the Dow Jones Industrial Average was down 52.78 points or 0.61 percent to 8549.87.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the Russian rouble crisis continues to dominate the international markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's the same old thing. It keeps kicking people in the face because they choose to ignore it, then the market runs up and it shows its ugly face again a few days later," said Jeff Milligan, an investment specialist at Priority Brokerage in Toronto.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Russian rouble dropped considerably in overnight trading, and the Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would not continue wide-scale \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This fall came one day after the government announced a short-term debt swap.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors bailed out of the Canadian dollar for safe-haven comfort of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . This sent the Canadian dollar to another new low. At noon it was trading at C$1.5600 (US$0.6410). The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, buying at levels of C$1.5560 (US$0.6426) to C$1.5595 (US$0.6412).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall in Toronto, 13 of the TSE 300's 14 subindexes were lower led by a 2.9 percent dip in the lightly weighted financial services sector. The group makes up only 1.5 percent of the overall index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Also leading the charge lower was the heavily weighted financial services group. It was down 1.7 percent while the paper and forest products group slipped 2.1 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the banking sector, Royal Bank of Canada  was off C$0.85 at C$64.90.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bucking the negative trend was the transportation sector basically flat at 0.01 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Oxford Properties Group Inc.  was the most heavily traded issue, rising C$0.60 to C$15.00 0n volume of 5.8 million shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ($1=$1.56 Canadian)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Scott Anderson, Reuters Toronto Newsroom, 416 941-8106, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8q01lcr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
