\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: C$ Plunges In Wake Of Dramatic Ruble Drop \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 15:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar plunged sharply lower Wednesday morning in a move that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers linked to the dramatic decline in the Russian ruble. \par \par \uc2  The sudden drop prompted repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which seemed to have some effect in containing the Canadian unit's decline. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5579 at 9:38 a.m. EDT (1338 GMT), from C$1.5549 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and C$1.5494 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  It reached the C$1.5590 area before shifting back lower after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market actions. \par \par \uc2  One London \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge was prompted by the continued collapse of the Russian ruble, which has depreciated about 69% against Deutsche mark since Tuesday's fixing. \par \par \uc2  "We're talking massive financial breakdown there," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Concerns that Russia will flood world with cheap commodities are swamping commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  all over the world, with several Scandanavian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also coming under sustained attack. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market focus has shifted away from Asia and mostly to Russia, the trader suggested. \par \par \uc2  "We were trading off (U.S.) dollar/yen for a long time, and now that market's just decoupled off of that," he said. "Since last Monday, when Russia announced that it had floated the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  essentially, it's been totally driven off that." \par \par \uc2  The trader said the push against the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have largely petered out in terms of Wednesday's action, but the downward pressure will resume in subsequent sessions. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, I think's it probably done the move for today," he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1341GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8q07aca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
