\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1998\par 14:49\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market repeatedly Wednesday morning,\par selling U.S. dollars at C$1.5560 and higher levels in an\par effort to smooth out trading action, said a trader in\par Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar leveled off briefly after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but started crawling higher shortly afterwards\par and was hovering at C$1.5575 at 8:45 a.m. EDT (1245 GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  starting selling the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par C$1.5560 and has been seen selling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at five-tick\par intervals up to about C$1.5580, the trader said.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets after intraday moves in either direction of\par 70 ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The U.S.\par dollar closed at C$1.5493 on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    In cases of sustained pressure against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par bank will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly at each five-tick level, and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players expected continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par long as the intense pressure remained on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday morning.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward\par pressure in recent sessions, setting an all-time lows on\par Monday and Tuesday, and then again this morning.\par    Analysts blame the sustained weakness in the Canadian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia.\par    The recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  problems in Russia have exacerbated\par the Canadian dollar's problems, since they are perceived as\par increasing the pressures on commodity-linked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-26-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0849EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8q0223k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
