\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1998\par 16:38\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday morning, selling U.S.\par dollars at C$1.5465 and C$1.5470, said a trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar showed little change as a result of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and had risen to C$1.5480 at 10:31 a.m. EDT\par (1431 GMT).\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  once again comes earlier than the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's usual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trigger.\par    The bank's unofficial policy is to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets after intraday moves in either direction of about 70\par ticks or more in order to contain volatility. The U.S.\par dollar closed at C$1.5417 on Friday, so the normal\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have been around C$1.5485.\par    In recent weeks, the bank has shifted to a more\par aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early on several\par occasions. At other times it has also employed the 70-tick\par rule.\par    In cases of sustained pressure against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly at each five-tick\par level.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market sources reported seeing a pattern of\par repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday morning.\par    They expected to see repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at each\par five-tick move by the U.S dollar.\par    Analysts blame the recent spate of weakness in the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia and other emerging markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-24-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1038EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8o0203i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
