\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 17:47\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par repeatedly in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market late Friday\par morning, selling U.S. dollars at least three times between\par C$1.5364 and C$1.5378 in an effort to contain volatility and\par ease pressure against the the Canadian dollar, traders in\par Toronto said.\par    Some traders said small to moderate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have\par been seen at C$1.5364, C$1.5371, and C$1.5378, and the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was expected to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at each\par five-tick level the U.S. dollar moves up Friday.\par    So far, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have merely slowed the U.S.\par dollar's ascent, as the U.S. unit was trading at C$1.5370 at\par 11:29 a.m. EDT (1529 GMT).\par    Friday's actions by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came after the U.S.\par dollar had recorded all-time highs against the Canadian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after soaring past the C$1.5355 level shortly after\par 10 a.m. EDT (1400 GMT), which was its previous historical\par high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Traders said that while relatively light, consolidative\par trading was initially expected for the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Friday, the U.S. dollar's overwhelming strength in global\par markets, and its topping of Y145.00 against the Japanese yen\par Friday flowed through with a strong U.S. dollar bid in\par Canada as well.\par    "It's all related to the U.S dollar/Japanese yen being\par extremely well bid, and the Mexican peso is getting creamed\par too," said a trader at a major Canadian bank in Toronto.\par "Emerging markets have turned to submerging markets, and\par Canada's not immune."\par    While the U.S. dollar is expected to continue to push\par higher, traders said more significant resistance exists at\par C$1.5385, which is a level that represents a value of 65\par U.S. cents for one Canadian dollar. Some analysts say the\par next significant target for the U.S. dollar is at C$1.5420.\par    The Bank of Canada's actions Friday came after it was\par absent from Thursday's session, and resumes its recent\par pattern of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early and unpredictably when the\par Canadian dollar slides against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . These\par tactics were initiated on Aug. 7, when the bank sold large\par amounts of U.S. dollars as the U.S. unit was trading at the\par C$1.5350 level.\par    The misgivings that many market players have voiced\par recently about the long-term effectiveness of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics are likely to grow, especially now that\par the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is trading at new all-time lows.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward\par pressure in recent months, prompting the more aggressive,\par activist \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics seen recently.\par    Analysts say the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fundamental\par weaknesses stemming from low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia and Russia.\par    The intense pressure on the Canadian dollar is expected\par to last until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or\par the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to defend the\par embattled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-21-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1147EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8l01z44\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
