\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Moves As C$ Falls To New Low \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 16:51\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday morning, selling U.S.\par dollars at C$1.5364 in an effort to smooth out trading\par action, said a trader in Toronto.\par    While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  momentarily halted the U.S.\par dollar's ascent, it quickly regained momentum, and was\par trading at C$1.5366 at 10:44 a.m. EDT (1444 GMT).\par    Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took place only minutes after the\par U.S. dollar had recorded new all-time highs against the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after soaring past the C$1.5355 level,\par which was its previous historical high. The amount of the\par bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was described by traders as moderate.\par    Traders said that while relatively light, consolidative\par trading was initially expected for the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par Friday, the U.S. dollar's overwhelming strength in global\par markets, and its topping of Y145.00 against the Japanese yen\par Friday flowed through with a strong U.S. dollar bid in\par Canada as well.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "It's all related to the U.S dollar/Japanese yen being\par extremely well bid, and the Mexican peso is getting creamed\par too," said a trader at a major Canadian bank in Toronto.\par "Emerging markets have turned to submerging markets, and\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's not immune."\par    The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comes after it was\par absent from Thursday's session, and resumes its recent\par pattern of intevening early and unpredictably when the\par Canadian dollar slides against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . These\par tactics were initiated on Aug. 7, when the bank sold large\par amounts of U.S. dollars as the U.S. unit was trading at the\par C$1.5350 level.\par    The misgivings that many market players have voiced\par recently about the long-term effectiveness of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics are likely to grow, especially now that\par the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is trading at new all-time lows.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward\par pressure in recent months, prompting the more aggressive,\par activist \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics seen recently.\par    Analysts say the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fundamental\par weaknesses stemming from low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia and Russia.\par    The intense pressure on the Canadian dollar is expected\par to last until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or\par the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to defend the\par embattled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-21-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1051EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8l01z0g\par }\page {\par\f