\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian dollar ends weaker despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 1,331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 22:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.5280/1.5355\tab ASIAN CLOSE    1.5280\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  US$ SUPPORT 1.5220 RESISTANCE 1.5400  HIGH 1.5315 LOW 1.5277 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN 1.5310 HIGH 1.5347\tab EUROPE OPEN    1.5308\par PREV CLOSE  1.5282 LOW  1.5308\tab HIGH 1.5314 LOW 1.5274\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WEDNESDAY, AUGUST 19\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TREND: WEAKER, ACTIVITY: LIGHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *Canada's dollar ended weaker at C$1.5334 (US$0.6521) despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . *Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seen in market to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.5341 (US$0.6518) in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par afternoon. *It stepped in from C$1.5321 (US$0.6527) to C$1.5328\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (US$0.6524) in morning. *Market awaiting Canada Supreme Court\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decision Thursday on whether Quebec can legally break away from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rest of Canada. *U.S. dollar slipped below 144 yen on growing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears. *\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  July CPI within\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations, at bottom of 1-3 percent target band. *Canada\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wholesale trade fell more than forecast by 1.7 percent in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *U.S. July housing starts came in stronger than expected,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising 5.7 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO, Aug 19 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar ended weaker at C$1.5334 (US$0.6521) on Wednesday despite several rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is again in the mood to sell the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with traders testing the topside of the U.S. dollar. Some speculators are talking about the possibility of a rise in Canadian interest rates, but that looks unrealistic given the low inflation rate and signs of slowing growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Afternoon trading was quiet following \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell U.S. dollars at C$1.5341 (US$0.6518). It touched a day's high of C$1.5347 (US$0.6516).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Dollar/Canada is still bid. (Traders) still want to take advantage of any pullbacks to buy (U.S.) dollars," one trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders are looking toward a record low of C$1.5355 (US$0.6513) set on August 7. If that level is breached, the next target will be C$1.5400 (US$0.6494), they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was cautious ahead of a Supreme Court decision on Thursday on the legality of any unilateral secession of the province of Quebec from the rest of the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The decision, which could be fairly detailed and complex,will be released at 0945 EDT/1345 GMT in Ottawa.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian dollar failed to benefit from the yen's steady rise overnight and in North American trade today. The U.S. dollar has been sliding this week against the yen, with traders now wary of holding long dollar positions at a time when Japan's top policymakers are suggesting that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) will not tolerate a further decline in the yen's value.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar stayed below 144 yen today, down from around 147 yen a week ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think the market focus is shifting back to the domestic situation. We could see a Quebec sovereignty risk increase after the Supreme Court ruling," said Rob Palombi, senior fixed-income analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Overnight you had a lot of talk about possible BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the Japanese yen... and that benefited other commodity-linked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , such as the Australian and New Zealand dollars, but the Canadian dollar continued to weaken."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara, dubbed "Mr Yen" for his influence on the market, on Wednesday continued to mount a verbal campaign to support the yen, warning traders of the risks of continually buying U.S. dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Risks of the stronger yen for investors are becoming bigger. They should be careful about that. Chances for yen-supportive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are drawing near," he told reporters in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In cross trading, the Canadian dollar slipped back to 1.1717 marks from 1.1790 marks at the previous close here, and extended losses to 93.84 yen from 94.75 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Canadian unit has been fluctuating in a range of 92-97 yen for the last two months. On a weekly chart basis, it has been on a general uptrend in the longer term since it bottomed out just above 60 yen in April 1995, when the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit record highs against key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Weakness returned to the local dollar this week as investors again bought U.S. dollars as a safe haven investment on renewed concern over Russia's financial system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Canada any rekindling of the war of words between pro-unity federalists and Quebec separatists might also scare overseas investors from holding Canadian assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's (today's weakness) the disappointment of the bank's actions on Monday," a senior trader at another bank said. "Yesterday they deviated from policy of metrical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the amount they spent was minimal and they had no impact at all."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The same players, the same bank accounts decided to sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this morning at C$1.5315 (US$0.6530), so we're in a very, very precarious situation. Even with good news coming out, that's not helping us," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market this week to slow the pace of the depreciation of the local dollar, at C$1.5303 (US$0.6535) and C$1.5296 (US$0.6538) on Tuesday and at every five points from C$1.5240 (US$0.6561) to C$1.5255 (US$0.6555) on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In trading since August 7, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been launching preemptive attacks on Canadian dollar selling, sometimes by buying the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively with large amounts of U.S. dollars. Monday was an exception when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  returned to its customary practice of waiting until the U.S. dollar moved 70-75 points from the previous close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economic indicators released this morning had little direct impact on price action in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's wholesale trade fell 1.7 percent on a seasonally adjusted basis in June from May. It was the first time since an economic slowdown in slowdown in 1995 that sales have fallen for two consecutive months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters survey of analysts had on average forecast a decline of 0.6 percent. The drop was predominantly due to shutdowns resulting from a General Motors strike in the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. July housing starts came in stronger than expected, marking the strongest pace in 11 years of a rise 5.7 percent to an annual rate of 1.718 million units after rising a revised 5.7 percent in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It was the fastest rate for any month since March 1987, when new hones were built at a rate of 1.73 million a year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Canada's consumer price index (CPI), a barometer of inflation, rose 1.0 percent year on year in July, at the same rate as in June. The core CPI (excluding food and energy prices) rose 1.3 percent year on year after a 1.0 percent rise in June. Economists on average had forecast the overall CPI would be up 1.1 percent and the core rate up 1.2 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Given the continuing slack in the economy, the greater risk is that inflation could move below the target band... as you eliminate the impact of the exchange rate," said Paul Ferley, assistant chief economist at Bank of Montreal. "We've had a fairly pronounced depreciation of the Canadian dollar, which is still putting upward pressure on the inflation measure. But that's only a transitory factor."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Looking at the bigger picture, Canada's second-quarter gross domestic product and current account data will be released on August 31. Canada will also release June retail sales on Thursday and June manufacturing shipments on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Masaru Sato, Reuters Toronto newsroom (416) 941-8107, toronto.newsroom@reuters.com))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8j012ps\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
