\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Late Morning: C$ Down, Approaching All-Time Low \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 16:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is down versus the U.S. dollar Wednesday morning, and is sliding towards the C$1.5350 level, which marks its all-time intraday low against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5330 at 10:47 a.m. EDT (1447 GMT), from C$1.5306 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and C$1.5275 late Tuesday. The Canadian dollar's slide drew two early morning rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to prevent it from falling further. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reported by traders to be selling moderate amounts of U.S. dollars at both the C$1.5320 and C$1.5328 levels. \par \par \uc2  Analysts attributed the Canadian unit's weakness Wednesday to renewed fears of Canadian political instability, along with a weak July inflation report that made an interest rate hike by the Bank of Canada to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seem even more remote. \par \par \uc2  Canada's Supreme Court will rule Thursday on on the legality of any future moves by the province of Quebec to secede from Canada, in a development that could lead to fresh political unrest in Canada. \par \par \uc2  Statistics Canada also reported earlier Wednesday that the consumer price index was unchanged in July from June, and up only 1.0% from July 1997, leading to a renewal of perceptions that it will be almost impossible for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates on economic grounds alone. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that with so many negatives stacked up against the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market players likely feel that its is safe to put more speculative pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent activist \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "It's the same players again taking a run at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not taking into account any of the good news such as a good stock market Tuesday and a strengthened Japanese yen," said Stephen Wateridge, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce in Toronto. "All the negatives are upsetting us and none of the positives are helping." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said that with two major \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  already completed Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely focusing on preventing a break by the U.S. dollar past the C$1.5350 to C$1.5385 range on Wednesday. Most did not rule out the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the remainder of the session. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 10:47 a.m. EDT (1447 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Tuesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5330      1.5306   1.5275\par    CDN/DEM     1.1755      1.1773   1.1787\par    CDN/YEN     93.87       94.23    94.84\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1450GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8j0717t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
