\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds Steady After Late Rally Erases Morning Losses \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 22:12\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds ended flat\par Wednesday, after a rally in the afternoon session enabled\par the market to recoup some of the steep losses recorded in\par morning trading.\par    5.00s 2000 99.50   unch     5.33% vs 5.33%\par    5.50s 2002 99.85   unch     5.54% vs 5.54%\par    6.00s 2008 102.89  dn 0.06  5.61% vs 5.61%\par    8.00s 2027 131.65  dn 0.10  5.74% vs 5.74%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-yr: +0.21 vs +0.15\par    CGB SEP 98 122.96 dn 0.04 volume 9,183\par    Analysts said a fresh spate of weakness in Canada's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , along with apprehension that a Supreme Court\par decision on Quebec separation expected Thursday could spark\par renewed political instability in Canada, left the market in\par the hands of only a few sellers in the morning session.\par    Some also cited rumors of large offshore sales of\par Canadian 10-year bonds from a single source as a factor that\par dealt overall sentiment a further blow.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    However, bonds gradually began inching back after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly to stabilize the\par Canadian dollar short of its all-time spot lows against the\par U.S. dollar, and after U.S. Treasurys also started to\par retrace some of their early losses.\par    "I suspect that given how spreads between Canada and the\par U.S. have widened, that's sufficient now to give us some\par support going forward," said David Yu, a portfolio manager\par at Perigree Investment Counsel.\par    Yu added that the selling seen Wednesday morning and in\par the previous two sessions may have discounted much of the\par concern over the supreme court's decision on Quebec's right\par to secede from Canada, which is expected at 9:45 a.m.\par Thursday.\par    "The market might have perceived that pessimism about\par Thursday's supreme court announcement is a little overdone,"\par he said. "Every time we have a Quebec uncertainty, the\par market always tends to go down before, and comes right back\par afterward."\par    Market watchers said trading is likely to remain very\par subdued at least until news of the Quebec decision hits the\par market Thursday morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-19-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1612EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1182 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8j021bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
