\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Repeated  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 16:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market repeatedly Wednesday morning, also selling moderate amounts of U.S. dollars at C$1.5328 in an effort to contain market volatility, traders in Toronto said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar leveled off briefly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and was trading at C$1.5325 at 10:25 a.m. EDT (1425 GMT). \par \par \uc2  The new round of U.S. dollar selling comes after an earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the C$1.5320 level failed to halt the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ascent toward its all-time intraday high of C$1.5350. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's actions also mark the ninth of the last ten sessions in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come out in support of the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The bank's actions thus far Wednesday have been typical of its recent policy of random, asymmetrical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as opposed to its previous unofficial policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only on intraday moves in either direction of 70 ticks or more. Tuesday's official U.S. dollar close was at C$1.5282. \par \par \uc2  Traders said total bank sales of U.S. dollars Wednesday morning have been somewhat higher than in previous days, and are likely intended to signal the bank's intention of preventing the U.S. dollar from advancing past the all-time high Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The bank's new strategy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  early and unpredictably began on August 7, when it sold large amounts of U.S. dollars as the U.S. unit was trading at the C$1.5350 level. \par \par \uc2  While the bank has generally been successful in preventing a further decline in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and minimizing outright speculative pressure against it, market players in recent days have begun to have misgivings about the long-term effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed to reverse the declining trend for the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and many feel the strategy is doomed unless backed by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move to lead interest rates higher. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward pressure in recent months, prompting the more aggressive, activist tactics seen recently. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fundamental weaknesses stemming from low commodity prices and global uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and financial turmoil in Asia and Russia. \par \par \uc2  The intense pressure on the Canadian dollar is expected to last until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to defend the embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-19-98 \par \par \uc2  1035EDT \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8j020vf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
