\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Afternoon: C$ Down, Holding Just Above All-Time Low \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 22:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar finished down against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, with only several rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  preventing the Canadian unit from crossing the C$1.5350 U.S. dollar level near its all-time spot low against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5328 at 4:24 p.m. EDT (2024 GMT), from C$1.5306 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT), and C$1.5275 late Tuesday. It rose as high as C$1.5343 at 2:06 p.m. EDT (1806 GMT) before being pushed back by U.S. dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said there were at least four main waves of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the day, taking place between C$1.5321 and C$1.5341. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said most of the pressure against the Canadian dollar Wednesday was the market's way of pricing in concerns that Thursday's Canada supreme court decision on the legal bases for Quebec seperation may lead to fresh political instability for Canada. \par \par \uc2  "The overall story behind the weakness was Quebec," said Mark Chandler, senior economist at Goldman Sachs in Toronto. "There was nothing much in the way of data, just the Quebec story and how that's playing out in the market." \par \par \uc2  The bank's tactics Wednesday seemed to some to be an attempt to impose a ceiling for the U.S. dollar around C$1.5350-C$1.5355, which represents both its all-time spot high against the Canadian dollar, and the level at which the bank first began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively on August 7. \par \par \uc2  But Chandler and others said this level is unlikely to be an absolute "line in the sand" for the bank, given the overall shroud of negativity hanging over the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think they still want to signal that they're more aggressive in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I'm not sure they're translating that to mean an absolute defense of C$1.5350," he said. "It would be kind of foolish to do that given their experience with defending absolute levels." \par \par \uc2  The ruling on Quebec seperation is expected to be announced by the Supreme Court at 9:45 a.m. (1345 GMT) Thursday, with potential volatile consequences for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 4:24 p.m. EDT (2024 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Tuesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5328      1.5306   1.5275\par    CDN/DEM     1.1724      1.1773   1.1787\par    CDN/YEN     93.82       94.23    94.84\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2030GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8j071rw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
