\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Morning: C$ Down, Approaching Key C$1.5300 Level \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 16:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is down early Tuesday against its U.S. counterpart, with trading mainly confined to a range below the C$1.5300 U.S. dollar level on uncertainty about the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  intentions. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.5292 at 10:15 a.m. EDT (1415 GMT), up marginally from C$1.5290 at 8:00 a.m. EDT (1200 GMT) and from C$1.5265 late Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in seven of the last eight trading sessions, must show its hand in a decisive way if it hopes to maintain the effectiveness of its tactics. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  early today," said Avery Shenfeld, senior economist at CIBC Wood Gundy Securities. "The market will be looking for an early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because we're getting closer to the point where they first stepped in to support the Canadian dollar a week and a half ago." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first aggressive, asymettrical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place near the C$1.5350 level on August 7, and some traders noted that despite the bank's support, the Canadian dollar is now edging back to the same levels. \par \par \uc2  "The view on Canada is still very negative, unless the bank is prepared to do something more concrete, like raising interest rates," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a Canadian bank. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't working - the bank is just spending money for nothing." \par \par \uc2  To add to the negative fundamentals pressuring Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some traders cited rumors that Russia may soon begin large-scale sales of base metals and other commodities in the wake of its de facto devaluation of the ruble, which would increase the competition for similar exports from Canada. \par \par \uc2  This would be expected to hurt Canada's export performance, which has already been relatively flat recently. \par \par \uc2  Statistics Canada reported earlier Tuesday that the nation's trade surplus widened slightly in June, to C$1.54 billion from C$1.33 billion in May, but with exports advancing only 0.1% over the previous month. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 10:15 a.m. EDT (1415 GMT), 8:00 a.m.\par EDT (1200 GMT), and late Monday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.5292      1.5290   1.5265\par    CDN/DEM     1.1751      1.1767   1.1759\par    CDN/YEN     95.12       95.32    95.58\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1418GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8i06znx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
