\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds End Down, Weighted By Continued C$ Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 22:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds extended their Monday losses with\par another session of thin, uneventful trading Tuesday, in which the\par renewed weakness in Canada's ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the dominant factor.\par    5.00s 2000 99.50   dn 0.05  5.33% vs 5.32%\par    5.50s 2002 99.85   dn 0.10  5.54% vs 5.54%\par    6.00s 2008 102.95  dn 0.20  5.60% vs 5.60%\par    8.00s 2027 131.77  dn 0.55  5.73% vs 5.71%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-yr: +0.20 vs +0.19\par    CGB SEP 98 123.00 dn 0.30 volume 5,728\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  considerations continue to outweigh the\par influence of all other factors, as there is still a near total lack of\par consensus concerning when and where the Canadian dollar will finally\par bottom out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  'It's being driven by the exchange rate, pure and simple, there's nothing else,' said Andrew Spence, senior economist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in Toronto. 'As long as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by changing short-term interest rates in response to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then it's up to the bond market to trade-off the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and put in whatever premium it feels is appropriate.' \par \par \uc2  Although trading in the Canadian dollar was similarly sluggish Tuesday, the U.S. dollar again briefly rose above C$1.5303 before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  returned it to a range below this level. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said that rebounds in North American equity markets also kept funds from flowing into bonds, but noted that Canadian bonds failed to catch much of a bounce even when money was fleeing declining stock markets over the past few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Market watchers said Wednesday's release of Canadian July consumer price data will likely be a non-event since inflation expectations are negligible at present, but some players are nervous about potential market volatility after Canada's supreme court hands down its ruling on the legality of potential Quebec separation on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  That decision is expected Thursday at 9:45 a.m. EDT (1345 GMT), while inflation data will be released Wednesday at 7:00 a.m. EDT (1100 GMT). \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  08-18-98 \par \par \uc2  04:37 PM \par \par \uc2  1182 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020010916du8i07max\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
