\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds End Down, Weighted By Continued C$ Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 22:37\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds extended their\par Monday losses with another session of thin, uneventful\par trading Tuesday, in which the renewed weakness in Canada's\par ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the dominant factor.\par    5.00s 2000 99.50   dn 0.05  5.33% vs 5.32%\par    5.50s 2002 99.85   dn 0.10  5.54% vs 5.54%\par    6.00s 2008 102.95  dn 0.20  5.60% vs 5.60%\par    8.00s 2027 131.77  dn 0.55  5.73% vs 5.71%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-yr: +0.20 vs +0.19\par    CGB SEP 98 123.00 dn 0.30 volume 5,728\par    Analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  considerations continue to\par outweigh the influence of all other factors, as there is\par still a near total lack of consensus concerning when and\par where the Canadian dollar will finally bottom out.\par    "It's being driven by the exchange rate, pure and\par simple, there's nothing else," said Andrew Spence, senior\par economist at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in Toronto.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  "As long\par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not going to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by changing\par short-term interest rates in response to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , then\par it's up to the bond market to trade-off the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and put\par in whatever premium it feels is appropriate."\par    Although trading in the Canadian dollar was similarly\par sluggish Tuesday, the U.S. dollar again briefly rose above\par C$1.5303 before \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par returned it to a range below this level.\par    Some traders said that rebounds in North American equity\par markets also kept funds from flowing into bonds, but noted\par that Canadian bonds failed to catch much of a bounce even\par when money was fleeing declining stock markets over the past\par few weeks.\par    Market watchers said Wednesday's release of Canadian\par July consumer price data will likely be a non-event since\par inflation expectations are negligible at present, but some\par players are nervous about potential market volatility after\par Canada's supreme court hands down its ruling on the legality\par of potential Quebec separation on Thursday.\par    That decision is expected Thursday at 9:45 a.m. EDT\par (1345 GMT), while inflation data will be released Wednesday\par at 7:00 a.m. EDT (1100 GMT).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-18-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1637EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1182 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8i0208h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
