\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Bank Seen Defending C$1.5300 \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 16:52\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday morning, selling U.S.\par dollars at C$1.5303 in an effort to smooth out trading\par action, said a trader in Toronto.\par    The U.S. dollar levelled off briefly after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and was trading at C$1.5277 at 10:47 a.m. EDT\par (1447 GMT).\par    Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  marks the eighth session out of\par the last nine that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has come out in support\par of the Canadian dollar.\par    While Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was more reminiscent of its\par previous unofficial policy of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets only on intraday moves in either direction of 70\par ticks or more, Tuesday the bank stepped in after the\par Canadian unit was only 40 ticks lower. Monday's official\par U.S. dollar close was at C$1.5263.\par    Traders described Tuesday's intevention amounts as\par moderate, and said the bank's intention for the interim is\par likely to keep the U.S. dollar from advancing above the\par C$1.5300 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The bank's new strategy of intevening early and\par unpredictably began on Aug. 7, when it sold large amounts of\par U.S. dollars as the U.S. unit was trading at the C$1.5350\par level.\par    While the bank has generally been successful in\par preventing a further decline in the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par minimizing outright speculative pressure against it, market\par players in recent days have begun to have misgivings about\par the long-term effectiveness of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tactics.\par    The Canadian dollar has been under severe downward\par pressure in recent months, prompting the more aggressive,\par activist tactics seen recently.\par    Analysts say the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fundamental\par weaknesses stemming from low commodity prices and global\par uncertainties stemming from the renewed economic and\par financial turmoil in Asia and Russia.\par    The intense pressure on the Canadian dollar is expected\par to last until the pressures originating in Asia relent, or\par the Bank of Canada raises interest rates to defend the\par embattled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  08-18-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1052EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4346 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8i01zom\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
