\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds Fall In Thin Trading On More  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds ended down Monday, as market\par sentiment was shaken by another bout of weakness in the Canadian dollar,\par following a week in which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had seemed to stabilize on the\par back of heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    5.00s 2000 99.55   dn 0.05  5.30% vs 5.28%\par    5.50s 2002 99.95   dn 0.10  5.51% vs 5.49%\par    6.00s 2008 103.16  dn 0.24  5.58% vs 5.54%\par    8.00s 2027 132.26  dn 0.44  5.70% vs 5.67%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-yr: +0.20 vs +0.17\par    CGB SEP 98 123.30 dn 0.19 volume 2,532\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said trading was sluggish throughout the session, as market\par players sat tight due to the weak dollar, potential controversy arising\par from U.S. President Clinton's afternoon grand jury testimony, and a\par heavy data calendar through the remainder of the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  'The market was off today more as a consequence of the weakness in the Canadian dollar than anything else,' said David Adamo, managing director of fixed-income research at Scotia Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  After being jolted lower overnight following Russia's de facto devaluation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Canadian dollar sunk further when North American trading opened, drawing several rounds of supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but only enough to slow its slide. \par \par \uc2  Adamo said Canadian bonds were also held back by a flat U.S. Treasurys market, which failed to advance when U.S. stock markets rallied and market players stayed on the sidelines to await news of Clinton's testimony. \par \par \uc2  Market watchers largely expect the rest of the week to be relatively bond friendly if the Canadian dollar can stabilize, as U.S. and Canadian inflation data to be released Tuesday and Wednesday, respectively, are expected to be benign, and no hawkish developments are expected to emerge from Tuesday's meeting of the U.S. Federal Reserve's Open Markets Committee. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  08-17-98 \par \par \uc2  04:32 PM \par \par \uc2  1182 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dj00000020010916du8h07io7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
