\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of Canada Tactics Win Praise, But Also Raise Questions \b0\par\par\uc2  By Don Curren \par \uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 22:02\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (Dow Jones)--While the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's feisty approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent sessions has helped bring some stability to the Canadian dollar - and has won plaudits from some market watchers - how long it will remain effective and how sustainable it is are open questions for Canadian dollar watchers. \par \par \uc2  After weeks of letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only as its usual policy dictates - when the U.S. dollar moves 70 ticks or more against the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the bank began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on Aug. 7, and followed the pattern every day last week except for Friday. \par \par \uc2  As a result of the bank's actions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been declining steadily for weeks, began to range trade. \par \par \uc2  Monday morning, after the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened significantly in the wake of the Russian ruble devaluation - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  let the U.S. dollar move the full 70 ticks before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That apparent reversion to the bank's standard operating procedure left some market watchers wondering if the bank has abandoned its more aggressive approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and will once again let the Canadian dollar slide, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only at 70-tick junctures. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts interviewed by Dow Jones Newswires believe the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  early if bank officials believe it is necessary. \par \par \uc2  But opinions were divided as to how long the bank's strategy will remain effective - and how long its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will permit it to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  early. \par \par \uc2  Andrew Pyle, vice president of investment banking at C.T. Securities Inc., said the bank's early \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may already be losing their effectiveness. \par \par \uc2  "Even the surprise element now, by doing this deviation tactic, isn't a lot," Pyle said. "I'd argue now that the market knows that the bank can do this, and does do this." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  08-17-98 \par \par \uc2  1602EDT \par \par \uc2  4219 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du8h01ywn\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (canada near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority) \cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbr